  "prompt": "By what date must an individual file the annual income tax return?",
  "runtimeCommit": "ba08ae790021ac1e22f438a82372a643dd886de0",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual must file the annual income tax return on or before April 15 of the following year after the taxable year.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe April 15 deadline applies to individuals, including citizens and resident aliens, who are required to report their income for the previous calendar year. If April 15 falls on a weekend or holiday, the deadline is typically extended to the next business day.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should ensure that their income tax returns are prepared and submitted by this date to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is advisable to keep accurate records throughout the year to facilitate timely and accurate filing.",
